   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7da2d79c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "This notebook shows how to build an Index compatible with `opr.inference.index`.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "fb89bd6a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import torch\n",
    "from torch import Tensor\n",
    "import open3d as o3d\n",
    "import MinkowskiEngine as ME\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "d078e105",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "DIST_THRESH = 0.5\n",
    "ANGLE_THRESH_DEG = 30\n",
    "\n",
    "POINTCLOUD_QUANTIZATION_SIZE = 0.05\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e8d59377",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The example below is for SberRobotics Office dataset.\n",
    "\n",
    "- `map1` - database, sampled with `DIST_THRESH` OR `ANGLE_THRESH_DEG`\n",
    "- The rest of the maps will be the queries"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "d5bcf8d5",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "root_data_dir = Path(\n",
